**Read:** [Cleaning and surface properties — Mauro Taborelli](../sources/Cleaning-and-Surface-Properties-Taborelli.lingua#r_1RDARBEFXDAW9Y2DNTJ2QBEP2E), detergent effects and special cases; [Cleaning technology in semiconductor device manufacturing VIII — ECS proceedings](../sources/Cleaning-Technology-in-Semiconductor-Device-Manufacturing-VIII.lingua#r_1CVF9XCJR7E3J37X5150BDS5Y2), material-loss and surface-conditioning studies.

The cleaning agent contacts everything exposed: substrate, oxide, coating, joint, seal and trapped region. Dissolution of an unwanted layer may accompany etching, swelling, leaching or redeposition elsewhere. A material's initial name does not specify its processed state or its acceptable change.

Distinguish removing a contaminant from intentionally stripping a layer. Define allowed dimensional, chemical, mechanical and functional changes before comparing methods. A bath can also acquire material from one workpiece and transfer it to the next.

**Work:** Make a compatibility account for a coated part with a joined second material. Follow the origin and destination of every measured element. Compare an unused coupon, a realistically aged part and a reused bath. Explain why a lower surface-contamination signal accompanied by a damaged coating cannot establish restored function.

**Return:** [Clean manufacturing and contamination control — from familiar objects to controlled processes](../Clean-manufacturing-and-contamination-control.lingua#r_7D8SQ8BVQDZQBDBGC6DP0JAMZN).
